{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "03", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "17", "M": "24", "S": "31"}}, "news": [{"title": "IndiQube Spaces\u2019 net loss narrows 80% to \u20b95.86 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "In the financial report for the quarter ending September 30, 2026, IndiQube Spaces disclosed a net loss after tax of \u20b95.86 crore. Despite this loss, total income surged to \u20b9492.16 crore, up from \u20b9366.59 crore compared to the same period last year. The company boasts 10.86 million square feet of managed space across 138 centres, serving 884 clients, revealing a positive trend in its financial performance for FY27.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/indiqube-spaces-net-loss-narrows-80-to-5-86-crore-in-q2-fy27/135503516?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-48718/135503516.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "Hyderabad: NCLT brings Madhapur land into Butta Infra liquidation estate", "para": "A significant piece of real estate located in Khanamet, Hyderabad, has been designated as part of the liquidation estate belonging to Butta Infrastructure. This decision stems from a ruling issued by the National Company Law Tribunal, which concluded that LIC Housing Finance did not adequately demonstrate its attempts at asset recovery.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/hyderabad-nclt-brings-madhapur-land-into-butta-infra-liquidation-estate/135503101?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-101694/135503101.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Ajmera Realty\u2019s net profit rises 48% to \u20b945.01 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "In Q2 FY27, Ajmera Realty & Infra India declared a remarkable 48.2 percent rise in net profit after tax. The firm's total income surged by 44.5 percent year-over-year. Despite this financial upswing, sales witnessed a notable decline, with collections down by 14 percent. However, the company made strides in reducing its debt by \u20b934 crore, which positively impacted its debt-to-equity ratio.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/ajmera-realtys-net-profit-rises-48-to-45-01-crore-in-q2-fy27/135502523?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-32300/135502523.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}